    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Flinders-Rural-Health-SA-Renmark--On-the-Traditional-Lands-of-the-First-Peoples-of-the-River-Murray--Mallee-Region/Associate-Professor-in-Rural-Health_JR0000017425": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in Rural Health",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Fixed Term until 31 December 2027 | Full-Time Academic Level D | $169,706 - $186,706 p.a. Location: Renmark | On the Traditional Lands of the First Peoples of the River Murray & Mallee Region View Position Description About the Role We are seeking an experienced and passionate academic leader to join the SA Rural Medical Program (SARM) as an Associate Professor in Rural Health, based in Renmark. This teaching-focused leadership role will drive excellence in clinical education, curriculum delivery and student learning across the rural medical program. Working closely with medical education leaders and academic staff, you will provide strategic direction, foster teaching innovation, and support the development of future rural medical practitioners while strengthening educational quality and program outcomes. You will also provide strong campus leadership and mentoring in our Renmark Campus. Key responsibilities include: Providing academic leadership and oversight of clinical teaching and learning across the SA Rural Medical Program, ensuring high-quality educational delivery and an exceptional student experience. Leading, mentoring and supporting academic and teaching staff, fostering a collaborative, high-performing culture and building capability in clinical education practices. Driving curriculum development, review and innovation, ensuring alignment with accreditation requirements, contemporary educational practices and the broader MD Program. Developing strong partnerships with healthcare providers, professional bodies and rural communities to enhance student opportunities, graduate employability and rural health outcomes. This position makes a significant contribution to the University’s strategic plan to change 10 million lives, Every One Matters , by 2035 through directly contributing to the strategic driver of Student Centric . By leading excellence in rural clinical education, enhancing the student learning experience, and supporting the development of future medical professionals, this role helps create meaningful pathways for student success while strengthening healthcare outcomes in rural and regional communities. About You You are an accomplished clinical educator and academic leader with a passion for developing the next generation of healthcare professionals. With extensive clinical expertise and a strong track record of excellence in tertiary teaching, you bring the leadership, innovation and collaborative approach required to enhance student learning, drive curriculum excellence, and support high-quality clinical education in a rural health setting. To be successful in this position, you will: Bring significant clinical expertise and professional credibility, supported by a doctoral qualification (or equivalent experience) and current or eligible registration with AHPRA. Have demonstrated excellence in tertiary teaching and clinical education, with a strong understanding of contemporary pedagogical practice and innovative approaches to learning and teaching. Show proven leadership experience in managing and mentoring academic teams, driving teaching innovation, and fostering a culture of collaboration, capability development and educational excellence. Excel at fostering meaningful relationships across the higher education and healthcare sectors, leveraging strong communication skills to drive successful program and accreditation outcomes. Flinders Rural and Remote Health SA Flinders Rural and Remote Health SA (FRRHSA) facilitates high quality multidisciplinary health education and research in our State's regional areas. We have a strong national and international reputation for providing community-engaged inter-professional training for medical, nursing, and allied health students. This includes the SA Rural Medical (SARM) program and multidisciplinary rural clinical placements. Through this practice, we bring new and exciting opportunities to actively engage and work with rural communities.  Life at Flinders They say know your place. We say you've found it right here. Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next. Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we’ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we’ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. So,  why work at Flinders? 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers  We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice  Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.  We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies. Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan   Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy   Prescribed Conditions for Employment Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. These include: Flinders University will require a current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. Staff working in a health care setting are strongly recommended to be fully vaccinated against COVID-19 in line with the SA Health policy. It is a requirement of this position that the incumbent maintain a current Working with Children Check which is satisfactory to the University in accordance with the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA). How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document.  This should be no more than 3 pages and address the Key Position Capabilities of the position description. Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged to participate fully and independently in the life of the University. If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please contact the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through recruitment@flinders.edu.au or call 08 8201 2383. For more information regarding this position, please contact Claire Drummond. Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 29 Sept 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
    },
    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Information-Security-Specialist_JR0000017422": {
      "title": "Information Security Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Details   Full-Time | Continuing Higher Education Officer Level 7 | $102,589 - $113,561 Location:  Bedford Park / Kaurna Country   View Position Description About the Role   We are offering an exciting opportunity for an Information Security Specialist within our Information and Digital Services Portfolio. Reporting to the Deputy Chief Information Security Officer, you will play a vital role in protecting the University's information assets, systems and infrastructure while contributing to the ongoing development of cyber security capabilities across a large and complex environment.   Working as part of a collaborative and highly skilled Information Security team, you will gain broad exposure across cyber security operations, infrastructure security, security monitoring, incident response, emerging cyber security threats and trends, and a diverse range of security projects. This role offers an excellent opportunity to deepen your technical expertise, expand your cyber security knowledge and contribute to meaningful outcomes in a supportive and flexible university environment, while helping strengthen the security of the University's critical systems and services.   Key responsibilities include: Configuring, deploying and maintaining security platforms and controls, including advanced email security, firewalls, intrusion prevention and detection systems, endpoint protection and VPN solutions. Providing technical advice on cyber security initiatives, security threats and emerging developments, while contributing to projects and activities that strengthen the University's security posture. Optimising and refining the University's proactive security monitoring capabilities to ensure cyber threats, incidents and vulnerabilities are identified, investigated and mitigated in a timely manner. Supporting and implementing security infrastructure and controls across the University's networks and systems, including incident response activities and collaboration with internal stakeholders to protect critical services and information assets. Promoting information security across the University through stakeholder engagement, guidance, project support and continuous improvement initiatives. A more comprehensive list of duties is available in the Position Description .   About You   You are a cyber security professional with strong technical capability and a genuine passion for information security. You enjoy working in a dynamic environment, solving complex problems and collaborating with others to deliver practical security outcomes. Whether your experience has been gained in higher education or another complex organisation, you are motivated by opportunities to learn, grow and broaden your exposure across multiple areas of cyber security. To be successful in this role, you will have: Relevant tertiary qualifications in Information Technology, Cyber Security or a related discipline, and/or equivalent professional experience. Demonstrated experience implementing, configuring and supporting cyber security technologies, including network security and monitoring solutions. Well-developed analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to assess risk and deliver practical security outcomes. Excellent communication and stakeholder engagement skills, including the ability to explain complex security concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences. Experience working within a complex IT environment and balancing security requirements with operational and business needs. About Information and Digital Services   Information and Digital Services (IDS) are a pivotal resource of the University, providing information and digital technology services and support to the Flinders University staff and student community. The IDS team apply technical expertise to support university projects and provide core services such as the IDS Service Desk, Audio visual, simulation and event services, Information security and identity access management services and more. Life at Flinders   They say know your place.  We say you've found it right here.    Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next.    Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we’ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we’ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create.    Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them.     So,  why work at Flinders?   17% Superannuation + salary packaging options   Flexible working arrangements   Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our  Thriving@Flinders  staff wellbeing program  Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers    We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards.   Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus  health care services ,  gym  and  childcare centre  (Bedford Park, South Australia).   Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment      Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.  We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies.   Please see here for our  Reconciliation Action Plan     Please see here for our  Indigenous Workforce Strategy        Prescribed Conditions for Employment   Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. This includes: A current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role.   How to Apply and Information   You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document.  This should be no more than 3 pages, and address the Key Position Capabilities of the  position description Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged to participate fully and independently in the life of the University. If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please advise the contact in the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through  recruitment@flinders.edu.au  or call 08 8201 2383.  For more information regarding this position, please contact  Tristan Bibbo Certification National Police Certificate - Australian Federal Police Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 16 Sept 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
    },
    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Flinders-Rural-Health-SA-Murray-Bridge--Ngarrindjeri-Country/Rural-Student-Services-Officer_JR0000017407": {
      "title": "Rural Student Services Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Full time | Fixed term until September 2027 Professional HEO5 | $84,599 - $93,366 p.a Location: Murray Bridge / Ngarrindjeri View Position Description About the Role As the Rural Student Services Officer, you will play a key role in creating an exceptional experience for students, staff and stakeholders across Flinders University's rural health programs. Based in Murray Bridge, this customer-focused position combines campus operations, student support, accommodation coordination and program administration to help deliver high-quality rural education and training opportunities. Working closely with the Rural Education Team and a broad range of internal and external partners, you will contribute to initiatives that strengthen rural health pathways and support the development of a skilled regional health workforce. Key responsibilities include: Delivering front-line student, staff and stakeholder support while ensuring a welcoming, safe and engaging rural campus environment. Coordinating the day-to-day operation of campus facilities, student accommodation, fleet vehicles, inventory and maintenance services across the Murray Bridge and Mallee region. Providing high-quality administrative support for rural teaching and learning activities, including the South Australia Rural Medical (SARM) Program, Rural Clinical School, Allied Health and Nursing placements, and Regional Training Hub initiatives. Building strong relationships with students, health professionals, community partners and internal stakeholders while supporting events, projects and initiatives that enhance the rural student experience and promote regional health careers. This position makes a significant contribution to the University’s strategic plan to change 10 million lives, Every One Matters, by 2035, through directly contributing to the strategic driver of being Student Centric, ensuring rural students receive high-quality support, access to learning opportunities, accommodation services and an engaging campus experience that enables their success and sense of belonging. About You You are a proactive and organised professional who thrives in a customer-focused environment and enjoys supporting students, staff and stakeholders to achieve positive outcomes. With strong administrative, communication and relationship-building skills, you can confidently manage competing priorities while contributing to a collaborative team culture. You are passionate about supporting rural communities and are motivated by the opportunity to enhance the student experience and help build a future regional health workforce. To be successful in this position, you will have: Strong administrative and organisational skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and exercise sound judgement when supporting students and stakeholders. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, enabling you to build effective relationships and liaise confidently with a diverse range of people. Proven ability to work collaboratively within a team, contribute to shared goals and deliver high-quality customer service. Experience coordinating activities, events or operational services, together with strong digital literacy and the ability to quickly learn new systems and technologies. Flinders Rural and Remote Health SA Flinders Rural and Remote Health SA (FRRHSA) facilitates high quality multidisciplinary health education and research in our State's regional areas. We have a strong national and international reputation for providing community-engaged inter-professional training for medical, nursing, and allied health students. This includes the SA Rural Medical (SARM) program and multidisciplinary rural clinical placements. Through this practice, we bring new and exciting opportunities to actively engage and work with rural communities.  Life at Flinders They say know your place. We say you've found it right here. Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next. Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we’ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we’ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. So,  why work at Flinders? 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers  We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice  Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.  We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies. Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan   Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy   Prescribed Conditions for Employment Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. These include: Flinders University will require a current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. Staff working in a health care setting are strongly recommended to be fully vaccinated against COVID-19 in line with the SA Health policy. It is a requirement of this position that the incumbent maintain a current Working with Children Check which is satisfactory to the University in accordance with the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA). How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document.  This should be no more than 3 pages and address the Key Position Capabilities of the position description. Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged to participate fully and independently in the life of the University. If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please contact the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through recruitment@flinders.edu.au or call 08 8201 2383. For more information regarding this position, please contact Tori Edmonds. Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 13 Sept 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
    },
